'' TKO0899 (fbc's 24 or 71) at a FIELD whose typedef is itself, as at a variable -- the
'' record had no layout and said nothing, so every use of it was TKO0994. A pointer is fine.
'' See symbols/declshape.tiko CheckFieldShape_.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/field-typedef-self.tiko
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: field-typedef-self.tiko(12,5): error TKO0899: 'uint8'
'' EXPECT-OUT: field-typedef-self.tiko(13,5): error TKO0899: 'uint16'
'' EXPECT-OUT: field-typedef-self.tiko(14,5): error TKO0899: 'uint32'
'' EXPECT-OUT: field-typedef-self.tiko(15,5): error TKO0899: 'uint64'
'' EXPECT-OUT: field-typedef-self.tiko(16,5): error TKO0899: 't'
'' EXPECT-OUT: field-typedef-self.tiko(17,5): error TKO0899: 'ta'
'' EXPECT-OUT: field-typedef-self.tiko(23,9): error TKO0899: 'uint8'
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0994
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 7
